course: dictionary
lesson: 15915
title: Unpaired: without a partner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unpaired means not in a pair, so it has no partner or match. The un- at the start means "not", and a pair is two things that go together. An unpaired sock is a sock whose matching sock is missing.
explain: «I found an unpaired sock under my bed.» There is no matching sock, so this one is on its own. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "a sock with no partner" makes sense, so you have got it right.
explain: Unpaired also has special meanings in maths and science. When you sort counters into twos and one is left over, that one is unpaired, which tells you the number is odd.
fact: Unpaired means not in a pair, without a partner or match.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unpaired is the opposite of paired.
fact: «Unpaired socks» are socks left without a matching sock.
fact: In maths, the counter left over when you make pairs shows that a number is odd.
fact: In science, an unpaired electron has no partner, and an unpaired organ, like the heart, has no matching twin in the body.
exercise: «I found an unpaired sock under my bed.» What does unpaired mean here? | Fast and clean | Very large | Dirty and wet | *Without a partner or match
exercise: When seven counters are sorted into pairs, one is left over. Why is that counter called unpaired? | *It has no partner | It is the biggest counter | It is the same colour as the others | It was dropped on the floor
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the opposite of unpaired. | loose | *paired | tidy | broken
test: In PE, Sam has no partner for the game, so Sam is unpaired. What does unpaired mean in this sentence? | Has the best score | *Has no partner | Is wearing a red top | Has run the furthest
test: Which of these is an unpaired part of the body? | *The heart | The left knee | The right ear | The left hand
exam: «Ten socks went into the wash, but one came out unpaired.» What does unpaired show? | It has been left in the sun | It is clean and dry | *It has lost its partner | It is the biggest sock
